[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue: the parser reads dates month first. The
reports in it hold two problems. Each now has its own ticket, and both are closed.

<Callout>
Closed 5 October. The parser is fixed. The booking-v3 form is retired, so its hint will not be fixed.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

- **parser** — the shared parser read every date month first. Our tenants write the day first,
  so 7 April came out as 4 July. Fixed in `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
- **hint** — the booking-v3 form printed `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field and then read the
  date day first. People did what the hint said, so their date flipped. The parser fix did not
  touch this form. The form is retired, so this one closes as won't fix.

## Why one ticket hid two

- We merged on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). Both
  problems produce the same subjects ("Wrong day on the invite", "Date is wrong"), so the
  subject cannot tell them apart.
- Intake tags come from the reporter's browser, not the tenant, so they cannot tell them apart
  either. The cause comes from the tenant: its locale and its booking form.
- The kb's own cause table found the hint problem and marked it "no ticket of its own". Nobody
  opened one.

## What to do next time

1. Before a big ticket is marked known, read its cause table. A second row is a second ticket.
2. Write a new decision record to replace 0001: merge on cause (tenant locale, booking form,
   channel), not on subject.

